codex
The case-split approach is sound but inefficient here: applying a conditional inner theorem makes the prover try to decide the recursive primality summary before it can use the theorem. I’m simplifying the source program itself in an equivalent Pythonic way—`count = count + is_prime` (Python booleans are integers)—so the already-proved general inner summary can flow through arithmetic as an SMT conditional, with no control-flow branch on an opaque Boolean.
apply patch
