codex
The remaining slowdown is symbolic recursion in the summaries themselves, not Python execution. I’m applying the skill’s prescribed fold orientation: keep the summaries exact but make the inductive equations fold a reached “next state” back to the current summary. This lets the loop circularity do the induction and prevents either summary from expanding on an unbounded symbolic input.
