The remaining failure is not the result—it is the invariant unnecessarily requiring and returning the exact final `count`. The task observes only the return value, and the loop guard already handles all counts. I’m removing those nonessential count constraints and existentially framing its final value; this also removes an SMT obligation about an opaque Boolean conditional that the return-value proof does not need.
